# /etc/mandaterail/state-release.env  (root:root 0600; used ONLY for manual `spend release`, never by a timer)
# R22-P3-1: mr_release is the only role with EXECUTE on mr_spend_release. mr_reconcile can only settle / mark ambiguous.
# R23: NO PASSWORD on the host. The mr_release password lives off-host (operator side) and is piped in at
# runtime with `--password-stdin` (see docs/ops/release-two-person.md). The URL below must not contain one.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://mr_release@127.0.0.1:5433/mandaterail
NETWORK=testnet
INDEXER_URL=https://testnet-idx.algonode.cloud
# R24-P2-1: a release needs a SECOND, independent provider (different host, genesis-checked).
# Blockdaemon (operator 3): PROOF2_URL=https://svc.blockdaemon.com/algorand/mainnet/native/indexer, PROOF2_KIND=indexer,
# PROOF2_TOKEN=<BLOCKDAEMON_API_KEY> (sent as X-API-Key). See docs/ops/mainnet-provider-blockdaemon.md.
# PROOF2_KIND = indexer | algod (algod = txId not in the pending pool + last-round; at least one
# provider must be an indexer). The Nodely host below is the same operator as algonode: acceptable
# for TestNet only. For MainNet use a provider run by someone else (or your own node).
# R25-P2-1: both hosts must be on the network's provider allowlist (mr_network_provider) with DIFFERENT
# operator ids. algonode + nodely are both operator "nodely", so with the pair below a proof-based release is
# REFUSED by the DB until a second operator is added (docs/ops/release-custody.md, "Provider allowlist").
PROOF2_URL=https://testnet-api.4160.nodely.dev
PROOF2_KIND=algod
